(ARG-43 — *(not a manual claim — a gap in the manual)* `last` never
 errors: with no user arguments it returns the program name, where
 `first` errors instead (ARG-42). The table says "Last argument" for
 `last` but "First user argument" for `first`, and that one word is the
 whole difference. See Discrepancy 2.
 The program name is the invocation path and cannot be diffed, so the
 probe asserts the identity `last is name` rather than printing it; it
 printed `./p` when run by hand with the command below.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-43.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   with no user arguments, last is the program name
   and empty is true at the same time
)
a text called ending is arguments's last.
On error print "last errored".
If ending is arguments's name then,
    Print "with no user arguments, last is the program name".
Otherwise,
    Print "with no user arguments, last is something else".
If arguments's empty then,
    Print "and empty is true at the same time".
